    "message": "fix(php): don't emit duplicate claims for a two-kind call\n\nSame root cause as the duplicate edge fixed earlier in this branch, on the\nclaim path this time, and it fires on ordinary untyped PHP rather than an\nexotic shape: phpCallKind splits the relationship dedup key, so\n`handle(); $obj->handle();` survives as two relationships. A claim carries no\nkind, so the two ops are byte-identical and nothing downstream can tell them\napart. Applied to both buildPatch and buildPatchWithResolution.\n\nContained today — stripMapModeOps drops all claims, so `ix map` never carried\nthese, and the only other consumer is a counter — but it inflates the counter\nand would double-assert on any path that keeps claims.\n\nAlso tightens the namespace-scoping perf test from a 10s to a 3s timeout: the\nfixed code runs in ~3ms and the old algorithm took ~12s, so 10s left only a\n1.2x margin over the thing it is meant to catch.\n\nMutation-tested. core-ingestion: 339 passed, 6 pre-existing failures unchanged.",
